IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `rra-part2-minimum-retirement-age`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- TESTS for Part 2.
-- Every expected value below is written from the text of the section named beside it,
-- before the assertion was run.

§ `Tests -- section 2(3), attaining an age`

-- s 2(3): the Nth anniversary of the date of birth.  Born 15 March 1960, the 63rd anniversary is 15 March 2023.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (Date 15 3 1960) 63 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2023)
-- Born on 29 February 1960 (a leap year): the 64th anniversary falls in 2024, a leap year, so 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (Date 29 2 1960) 64 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- The 63rd anniversary falls in 2023, which has no 29 February, and the Act does not say which date stands in: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (Date 29 2 1960) 63 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "N years of age (where N is a positive integer)": zero is not an N.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the date of the anniversary on which the person attains the age` (Date 15 3 1960) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- "on or after the Nth ... anniversary": the day before the anniversary is not yet, the anniversary itself is.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person has attained the age on the date` (Date 15 3 1960) 63 (Date 14 3 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person has attained the age on the date` (Date 15 3 1960) 63 (Date 15 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person has attained the age on the date` (Date 15 3 1960) 63 (Date 16 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person has attained the age on the date` (Date 29 2 1960) 63 (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 4(1), what the Minister may specify`

-- "which must be at least 62 years but not more than 65 years", specified "by notification in the Gazette".
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the age specified may be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 62 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the age specified may be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 65 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the age specified may be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 61 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the age specified may be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 66 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Within the range but not specified by notification in the Gazette: the grant is limited by its own wording.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the age specified may be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 63 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outside the range: the range decides, whatever the manner.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the age specified may be the prescribed minimum retirement age` 66 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 4(2), no dismissal on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- Born 1 January 1960 with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63: the employee attains it on 1 January 2023.
`an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

-- The day before the age is attained, on the ground of age: the Act says the employer must not.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the employer may dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` TRUE (Date 31 12 2022) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same, though a contract of service says the employer may: "Despite ... contract of service", the answer does not change.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the employer may dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` TRUE (Date 31 12 2022) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- On the day the age is attained the employee is no longer "before" it: outside the section's wording.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the employer may dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not on the ground of age: outside the section's wording.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the employer may dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` FALSE (Date 31 12 2022) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative twin.  The clock starts on 1 December 2022; the age is attained on day 31 (1 January 2023).
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACH  (dismissed on day 30, 31 December 2022, the day before the age is attained)
#TRACE `s 4(2) the employer shall not dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 12 2022) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `dismiss the employee on the ground of age` AT 30
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (dismissed on day 31, the day the age is attained)
#TRACE `s 4(2) the employer shall not dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 12 2022) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `dismiss the employee on the ground of age` AT 31
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (nothing happens)
#TRACE `s 4(2) the employer shall not dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 12 2022) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (the age was attained before the clock started: nothing to prohibit)
#TRACE `s 4(2) the employer shall not dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 1 2 2023) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `dismiss the employee on the ground of age` AT 5

§ `Tests -- section 4(3), the offence and its penalty`

#ASSERT `s 4(3) the employer is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the employer is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the penalty on conviction` EQUALS (Penalty OF 5_000, 6)
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the sentence is within the penalty` TRUE 5_000 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the sentence is within the penalty` TRUE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the sentence is within the penalty` TRUE 5_001 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the sentence is within the penalty` TRUE 5_000 7 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No conviction: the employer is "liable on conviction" only.
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the sentence is within the penalty` FALSE 5_000 6 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 6, a term below the prescribed minimum retirement age`

-- Prescribed minimum retirement age 63.
#ASSERT `s 6 the term is void` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` TRUE 62 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the term is void` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` TRUE 63 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 the term is void` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` TRUE 65 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a term of a contract of service or collective agreement: outside the section.
#ASSERT `s 6 the term is void` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` FALSE 62 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "void to the extent that it is so less favourable": a term of 62 stands as 63; a term of 65 is untouched.
#ASSERT `s 6 the retirement age that the term leaves standing` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` 62 EQUALS 63
#ASSERT `s 6 the retirement age that the term leaves standing` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` 63 EQUALS 63
#ASSERT `s 6 the retirement age that the term leaves standing` `an employee who attains the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023` 65 EQUALS 65

